        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: meaning before machinery",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Comes can assert “you eat.” Quiero que comas presents your eating as what I want. The e becomes a contrast helps you hear the two meanings. It does not mean that every a form is subjunctive; use the learned frame as a whole."
            }
          ]
        },
